# local/ — per-user profile dirs (template: local/example/ is tracked in git).
#
# Layout (fixed basenames per profile):
#   local/<name>/secrets.sh   every shell (env, PATH; scripts too)
#   local/<name>/login.sh       login zsh only
#   local/<name>/aliases.sh     interactive aliases
#   local/<name>/tools.sh       per-tool hooks (after compinit)
#   local/<name>/company.sh     work / employer env (interactive, last)
#
# Root files:
#   local/active                one line: profile name (dotfiles use <name>)
#   local/disabled              module toggles (dotfiles disable <profile>)
#
# Quick start:
#   cp -r local/example local/gfs
#   dotfiles use gfs
#   exec zsh
#
# local/example/ is the tracked template. Real profiles (gfs/, etc.) and
# local/active are gitignored. Keep drop-ins SILENT (no echo).
